--- a/docs/usage.md
+++ b/docs/usage.md
@@ -6,3 +6,18 @@ ends.
 
 `unique_slug(title, taken)` does the same and then appends `-2`, `-3`, … until
 the result is not already in `taken`.
+
+## Collisions
+
+`taken` is any container supporting `in`. The desk passes the set of slugs
+already used in the same section, which is the scope the CMS enforces
+uniqueness over — two sections may hold the same slug.
+
+The counter starts at `-2` because the first article keeps the bare slug. There
+is no upper bound on the counter; in practice the desk has never gone past
+`-4`.
+
+## What is not handled
+
+Transliteration is ASCII-folding only, so a Cyrillic or Greek headline folds
+away to an empty string and the caller gets `''`. The desk types those by hand.
